# SPA-Net + ParT Resource-Aware Comparison Contract

Status: FROZEN DECISION
Date: 2026-09-03

## Scientific question

Does adding a frozen constituent-level Particle Transformer
representation to each reconstructed AK4 jet improve the existing
SPA-Net HH→4b reconstruction/classification baseline?

## Governing baseline

Model: SPA-Net 10M
Training budget: 50 epochs
Initialization: historical governing run
Input object: reconstructed AK4 jets
Maximum jet slots: 10

Native per-jet features:
1. pT
2. eta
3. phi
4. mass
5. probB
6. probC
7. probL

Input width: 7 features / jet

Governing checkpoint SHA256:

fd9ea100825ecc0412a2666f01fd19d1a91b25a50109b958c307102fa6943de5

This checkpoint remains frozen and MUST NOT be modified or replaced.

The completed 75-epoch study did not improve upon this governing
50-epoch baseline, so no additional native-feature SPA-Net retraining
is planned for the primary resource-aware comparison.

## New model

Model: SPA-Net + frozen ParT embeddings

SPA-Net initialization: FRESH
SPA-Net training budget: 50 epochs

Per-jet input:

    7 native reconstructed-jet features
    +
    128-dimensional frozen ParT embedding

Total input width:

    135 features / jet

ParT checkpoint SHA256:

61e752f80d7c237d4b18b97705df416a8518dd9e3d5a78a8bbdeebadd787fec0

ParT provenance:
official JetClass-supervised Particle Transformer checkpoint,
not the PKU jetfree-hh4b event-level classifier.

ParT is FROZEN:
- no gradient updates
- no fine-tuning
- no ParT inference inside SPA-Net epochs
- precomputed per-jet embeddings are consumed from the frozen
  embedding dataset

## Quantities held fixed

The new SPA-Net+ParT run should match the governing 50-epoch SPA10M
training contract wherever technically applicable:

- same train/validation cohorts
- same event identities
- same seed
- same 50-epoch budget
- same optimizer
- same learning-rate schedule
- same reconstruction targets
- same classification targets
- same task/loss weighting
- same jet ordering
- same 10-jet maximum
- same native-feature preprocessing
- same downstream SPA-Net architecture/hidden dimensions where possible

## Intentional model difference

Baseline:

    SPA-Net(native_7)

New model:

    SPA-Net(native_7 + frozen_ParT_128)

No second fresh native-only SPA-Net control is planned.

This is intentionally a RESOURCE-AWARE comparison against an existing
frozen and audited governing baseline, rather than a contemporaneous
two-run ablation.

## Training gate

SPA-Net+ParT training MUST NOT begin until:

- 880/880 train ParT H5 shards are valid
- 880/880 train receipts are valid
- 220/220 validation ParT H5 shards are valid
- 220/220 validation receipts are valid
- train_0384 has been regenerated/canonicalized with a valid receipt
- all 15 wrapped-window repair shards pass final validation
- native-event ↔ ParT-event identity closure passes
- native-jet ↔ ParT-jet identity closure passes
- ParT embedding dimension is exactly 128
- no nonfinite embeddings are present
- joined tensor/mask audit passes
- relevant code/config/checkpoint hashes are frozen

## Evaluation

Compare the frozen baseline and the new SPA-Net+ParT model using the
same evaluation machinery, including where applicable:

- validation average jet accuracy
- validation loss
- Higgs assignment performance
- event classification performance
- ROC/AUC
- fixed signal-efficiency background rejection
- downstream Z_A
- downstream B95

## Explicit non-goals

For the primary comparison:

- DO NOT retrain a second native-only SPA-Net control
- DO NOT fine-tune the frozen 50-epoch SPA-Net checkpoint
- DO NOT fine-tune ParT
- DO NOT substitute the 75-epoch SPA-Net checkpoint
- DO NOT change the dataset split
